: 1, "explanation": "The OBT serves as a central time reference for various operations like commanding, sequencing, and telemetry stamping, ensuring consistent timing across the spacecraft's systems.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_11.wmf"}, {"question": "Which of the following operations utilizes OBT-based commanding?", "options": ["Payload Sequencer", "Orbit Coefficient Uplink", "Memory dump", "All of the above"], "correct": 3, "explanation": "OBT-based commanding is used in several operations including Payload Sequencer, Orbit Coefficient Uplink, and Memory dump initiation, as described in the slide content.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_11.wmf"}, {"question": "What is the role of OBT in the context of Orbit Coefficient Uplink?", "options": ["It is used to timestamp the state vectors", "It is used to convert the epoch time to a format suitable for onboard processing", "It is used to encrypt the state vectors", "It is used to compress the data for efficient transmission"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "The epoch time associated with the state vectors is converted to OBT and uplinked along with the state vectors, making OBT crucial for their proper application onboard.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_11.wmf"}, {"question": "How is telemetry (TM) frame stamping performed?", "options": ["Using the ground station's time", "Using the OBT", "Using the UTC time", "Using a separate onboard clock"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "The slide explicitly states that telemetry frame stamping is done using the OBT, ensuring consistency with other onboard timing mechanisms.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_11.wmf"}, {"question": "What is the primary purpose of the drift estimation module in the context of TT&C security?", "options": ["To compensate for GPS signal loss", "To estimate and compensate for on-board time drift", "To track satellite trajectory", "To secure communication channels"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "The drift estimation module is designed to estimate and compensate for time drift caused by various factors affecting the crystal oscillators, ensuring accurate timekeeping for TT&C systems.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_12.wmf"}, {"question": "Which of the following is identified as a major drift factor in crystal oscillators?", "options": ["Humidity", "Initial Drift", "Electric fields", "Pressure"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "Initial Drift, caused by manufacturing imperfections, is explicitly listed as a major drift factor. Humidity, pressure, and electric fields are either mitigated by hermetic sealing or classified as minor factors.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_12.wmf"}, {"question": "What is the total time (Ttotal) calculated as in the context of OBT-Correlation with GRT for Convolutional Encoding?", "options": ["Tformat + Tenc + Trand + Tmod + Tdemod", "Tformat + Tenc + Trand + Tmod + Tdemod + Tdecod", "Tformat + Tenc + Trand + Tmod", "Tformat + Tenc + Trand + Tmod + Tdemod + Tdecod + additional processing time"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "Ttotal includes all the components mentioned in the slide: Tformat (Frame Header generation, Encryption, CRC computation, Sampling of Frame), Tenc (Convolutional Encoding), Trand (Randomization), Tmod (Sub-Carrier Modulation & IF Modulation), Tdemod (IF Demodulation & Sub-Carrier Demodulation), and Tdecod (Viterbi Decoding).", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_14.wmf"}, {"question": "When can GRT stamping be performed in the ground chain for Convolutional Encoding?", "options": ["Before encoding", "After encoding but before decoding", "After decoding", "At any time during the process"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "The slide notes that in the ground chain, Frame Sync is only visible after the decoding operation. Therefore, GRT stamping can only be done after decoding, necessitating that decoding latency be considered in the correlation.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_14.wmf"}, {"question": "What method is used for Viterbi Decoding in the context of Convolutional Encoding?", "options": ["Register Exchange method", "Traceback method", "Register Exchange/ Traceback method", "None of the above"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "The slide explicitly mentions that Viterbi Decoding uses the Register Exchange/ Traceback method.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_14.wmf"}, {"question": "Why is compressing telemetry data considered beneficial for satellites?", "options": ["It increases the amount of science data that can be transmitted", "It reduces the impact of channel errors on housekeeping data", "It decreases the required on-board storage space", "It simplifies the overall system architecture"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "Compression reduces the storage space needed for telemetry data on the satellite, which is a key benefit.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_15.wmf"}, {"question": "Which of the following is a challenge associated with compressing telemetry data?", "options": ["Increased complexity of the satellite system", "Reduced impact of channel errors on housekeeping data", "Higher transmission power requirements", "More efficient use of bandwidth"], "correct": 0, "explanation": "Compression adds complexity because it requires on-board compression and ground-based decompression, making the system more intricate.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_15.wmf"}, {"question": "In which type of mission is telemetry data compression particularly useful?", "options": ["High-power satellites with ample bandwidth", "Deep space missions with limited power", "Satellites with minimal housekeeping data", "Missions where science data is negligible"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "Deep space missions often face power and bandwidth constraints, making compression beneficial for optimizing resource usage.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_15.wmf"}, {"question": "What is a potential consequence of losing a frame of compressed housekeeping data?", "options": ["Minimal impact on the overall data", "Significant impact due to higher data density", "No impact as data can be easily reconstructed", "Reduced need for error correction"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "Compressed data is more sensitive to loss because the loss of a single frame can represent a larger amount of original data, amplifying the impact.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_15.wmf"}, {"question": "What is the primary purpose of spoofing in the context of spacecraft TT&C links?", "options": ["To jam satellite signals", "To impersonate an authorized source to send false telecommands or modify telemetry data", "To physically damage the spacecraft's payload system", "To increase the strength of GNSS signals"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "Spoofing involves impersonating a legitimate source to send false commands or alter telemetry data, not jamming or physical damage.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_16.wmf"}, {"question": "What were the consequences of the GPS spoofing incident near Novorossiysk in 2017?", "options": ["Ships experienced complete loss of navigation", "Ships reported false positions on digital maps, while being stationary in the harbor", "Ships successfully detected and neutralized the spoofing attack", "The spoofing attack caused permanent damage to the affected vessels' GNSS receivers"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "The vessels' navigation systems were deceived into displaying false positions, while their actual location remained unchanged.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_16.wmf"}, {"question": "Which of the following is NOT a listed anti-spoofing protection measure?", "options": ["Encryption", "Authentication", "Following CCSDS security standards", "Using stronger GNSS signals"], "correct": 3, "explanation": "Using stronger GNSS signals is not explicitly mentioned as an anti-spoofing measure in the provided content. The listed measures are encryption, authentication, and following CCSDS security standards.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_16.wmf"}, {"question": "What is the primary purpose of jamming in spacecraft TM/TC links?", "options": ["To improve communication quality", "To enhance data transmission rate", "To deny communication between ground transmitter and on-board receiver", "To increase signal strength"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "Jamming is defined as the intentional transmission of interfering radio signals to disrupt communication between the ground transmitter and the spacecraft's on-board receiver.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_17.wmf"}, {"question": "Which type of jamming targets a specific frequency channel?", "options": ["Uplink Jamming", "Downlink Jamming", "Spot Jamming", "Barrage Jamming"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "Spot jamming is the type of jamming that specifically targets a particular frequency channel, making it difficult to communicate on that channel.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_17.wmf"}, {"question": "What was the primary method used for GPS/GNSS jamming in the Baltic Region between August 2023 and March 2024?", "options": ["Satellite-based jamming only", "Ground-based jamming only", "Both ground-based and space-based or airborne assets", "Low-power jamming signals"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "The slide states that the interference was caused by high-power jamming utilizing both ground-based jammers and potentially space-based or airborne assets.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_18.wmf"}, {"question": "What was the impact of the GPS/GNSS jamming on air traffic control in the Baltic Region?", "options": ["Increased efficiency in navigation", "Improved satellite signal reception", "Widespread GPS outages forcing reliance on backup systems", "Enhanced security measures"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "The slide mentions that air traffic control in Finland, Estonia, and Latvia reported widespread GPS outages, forcing airplanes to rely on backup navigation systems.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_18.wmf"}, {"question": "How long was the most intense period of GPS/GNSS jamming in March 2024?", "options": ["24 hours", "48 hours", "63 hours", "72 hours"], "correct": 2, "explanation": "The slide specifies that a 63-hour period of intense jamming affected over 1,600 aircraft in March 2024.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_18.wmf"}, {"question": "What is the primary focus of the Telemetry, Tracking, and Command (TT&C) Security in the context of spacecraft systems?", "options": ["Data transmission speed", "Encryption and authentication protocols", "Orbit determination", "Payload management"], "correct": 1, "explanation": "TT&C Security primarily deals with securing communication between ground stations and spacecraft, which includes encryption and authentication to prevent unauthorized access and data breaches.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_19.wmf"}, {"question": "Who is scheduled to continue the discussion on the topic of Spacecraft Telecommand System, Encryption & Authentication?", "options": ["Mr. Rajagopalan", "Mr. Sharma", "Mr. Patel", "Mr. Kumar"], "correct": 0, "explanation": "The slide explicitly states that the topic will be continued by Mr. Rajagopalan.", "image": "C:\\Users\\Kriteesh Parashar\\Downloads\\inspace-cybersecurity\\slide_images\\l7pre\\slide_19.wmf"}];
    let currentIdx = 0;
    let correctCount = 0;
    let answeredCount = 0;

    const qText = document.getElementById('q-text');
    const qImg = document.getElementById('q-img');
    const optionsContainer = document.getElementById('options-container');
    const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submit-btn');
    const nextBtn = document.getElementById('next-btn');
    const ticker = document.getElementById('ticker');
    const explanation = document.getElementById('explanation');

    function loadQuestion() {
        const q = quizData[currentIdx];
        qText.innerText = q.question;
        
        if(q.image) {
            qImg.src = q.image;
            qImg.classList.remove('hidden');
        } else {
            qImg.classList.add('hidden');
        }

        optionsContainer.innerHTML = '';
        q.options.forEach((opt, i) => {
            const btn = document.createElement('button');
            btn.className = 'option-btn';
            btn.innerText = opt;
            btn.onclick = () => selectOption(i);
            optionsContainer.appendChild(btn);
        });

        explanation.classList.add('hidden');
        submitBtn.disabled = true;
        nextBtn.disabled = true;
        updateTicker();
    }

    let selectedIdx = null;
    function selectOption(idx) {
        if (nextBtn.disabled === false) return; // Lock after submit
        selectedIdx = idx;
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
        
        // Visual feedback for selection
        Array.from(optionsContainer.children).forEach((btn, i) => {
            btn.style.background = (i === idx) ? '#e9ecef' : 'white';
        });
    }

    submitBtn.onclick = () => {
        const q = quizData[currentIdx];
        const buttons = optionsContainer.children;
        
        // Requirement 5: Highlight correct in green
        buttons[q.correct].classList.add('correct');
        
        if (selectedIdx === q.correct) {
            correctCount++;
        }
        
        answeredCount++;
        explanation.innerText = "Explanation: " + q.explanation;
        explanation.classList.remove('hidden');
        
        submitBtn.disabled = true;
        nextBtn.disabled = false;
        
        if (currentIdx === quizData.length - 1) {
            nextBtn.innerText = "Done";
        }
        updateTicker();
    };

    nextBtn.onclick = () => {
        if (currentIdx < quizData.length - 1) {
            currentIdx++;
            loadQuestion();
        } else {
            showFinal();
        }
    };

    function updateTicker() {
        ticker.innerText = `Correct: ${correctCount} / Answered: ${answeredCount} / Total: ${quizData.length}`;
    }

    function showFinal() {
        document.getElementById('quiz-container').classList.add('hidden');
        const final = document.getElementById('final-screen');
        final.classList.remove('hidden');
        document.getElementById('final-score').innerText = `Your Score: ${correctCount} / ${quizData.length}`;
    }

    loadQuestion();
</script>
